                   To continue prefix processing for the family of all permutations, we need expected/summed effect
                   of consuming one missing number. The standard way is to track aggregate rank sum term for future
                   fixed numbers. We do that via BIT of missing ranks.
                */

                z--;
            }
        }
    }

    /* The above computes sum of 0-based lexicographic indices.
       Add number of valid permutations to convert to 1-based page numbers.
    */
    ll valid = fact[K];
    ans = (ans + valid) % MOD;

    printf("%lld\n", ans % MOD);

